From 62f8439fdebc44a4e5a82e4e3791c729d6c635a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] fix(trace): trace control hints say what the tracer
 does (ADR-396)

Every numeric trace control now has a hint checked against the engine:
Cutoff and Threshold describe the inclusive brightness band; Remove ink
specks and Ignore Less Than say that pixels touching at a corner count as
one mark; Smoothness and Optimize describe corner rounding and point
merging; Edge Sensitivity says how much darker than its surroundings a
mark must be; Edge Detail names the neighbourhood size (about 25 px at 0
to 6 px at 100) instead of claiming to smooth noise; Minimum line says
holes inside shapes are kept. The alpha-mask note says opacity is read as
brightness, 0 for fully opaque.

Area fields step in whole pixels and round what is typed, so a field no
longer shows 2.5 while the tracer uses 3. A Cutoff above Threshold now
shows which pixels the band selects (the tracer orders the two ends).

Edge Sensitivity is shown from the low ratio the detector reads, and
changing it writes only that ratio. The high ratio and the join gap that
Sensitivity and Detail used to rewrite have no reader in the detector.
The unreachable Sensitivity 50 and Detail 68 fallbacks are removed; the
default preset still shows Sensitivity 44 and Detail 68.

The number row moves to TraceNumberRow.tsx with an explicit hint and
unit, and the hint texts to trace-setting-hints.ts.

Expectations updated in trace-options.test.ts: Sensitivity and Detail no
longer change edgeHighThresholdRatio or edgeJoinGapPx, because nothing
reads them. New tests check the displayed Sensitivity for every value,
whole-pixel rounding, and the swapped-band note against the traced ink.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
